      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The character could exploit the very concept of *familismo*, using deep-seated loyalty to manipulate trust within their community. They might use established family or neighborhood connections as a vetting system for their victims, making the fraud feel like a trusted business deal rather than a scam. This allows them to operate under a veil of cultural familiarity, making their deception far more insidious to those who rely on those same community bonds.",
