      "content": "That makes a lot of sense for the psychological depth of the show. To really nail the 'gritty realism' part, I want to look at the landscape they're operating in. When we look at how these types of high-level schemes develop, is there a correlation between these specific cultural social structures and the level of organized, systematic criminality we might see? Like, does the emphasis on tight-knit community ties naturally lend itself to more structured, perhaps even more aggressive, criminal operations compared to, say, a white-collar criminal from a more individualistic background? I'm trying to figure out if I should frame their criminal organization as something that feels more like an extension of a certain type of cultural communalism.",
